From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: avoid full AHB teardown before registration

An AHB device can bind while its QMI firmware service is still absent.
Full core teardown assumes later resources exist. Use the REGISTERED
boundary already present in the shutdown callback, and drain queued
initialization work before choosing the partial cleanup path.
The registered path retains its existing full teardown sequence.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -1320,14 +1320,17 @@
 {
 	struct ath11k_base *ab = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags)) {
+	ath11k_ahb_remove_prepare(ab);
+
+	/* Probe can finish before the firmware service creates the radios. */
+	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags) ||
+	    !test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags)) {
 		ath11k_ahb_power_down(ab, false);
 		ath11k_debugfs_soc_destroy(ab);
 		ath11k_qmi_deinit_service(ab);
 		goto qmi_fail;
 	}
 
-	ath11k_ahb_remove_prepare(ab);
 	ath11k_core_deinit(ab);
 
 qmi_fail:
